hich expects banker's rounding per FIN-212. round_money was using ROUND_HALF_UP.\n\nChange: switch the quantize rounding mode in src/money.py from ROUND_HALF_UP to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. The docstring already described half-even behavior.\n\nVerification: CI run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n\nNeeds code-owner approval before merge (main is protected).", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-half-even-rounding-pr-1"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101, but I did not merge it. Policy requires code-owner approval before anything merges into main, and I have no approval yet.\n\n- **Fix:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` now uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The docstring already described half-even, so the code now matches it.\n- **Branch:** `fix/fin-212-half-even-rounding`, commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101 targets `main` and requests review from `code-owner`. The URL is https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nTo ship in today's release, a code owner needs to approve PR #101. Once they do, I can merge it.", "type": "text"}]}]}